# What each entry shows: every value its view states of it and every value its members' current versions state of the
# fields the view shows, each with From, the member whose current version states it, and Lead, whether that member is
# the entry's lead (cascade:leadMember), whose values come first. An entry is what an app shows: one allergy, one
# condition, one vaccination; no merged record is stored, so the view holds each member's current values as a node of
# its own (cascade:memberCurrentValues) and this reads the view alone. The view takes the entry's name and codes from
# its lead, and its status and dates from the members the derivations chose for them (cascade:statusFrom,
# cascade:dateFrom and, for a medication, cascade:medicationUseStartDateFrom, cascade:prescriptionWrittenDateFrom and cascade:dosageFrom, and for an allergy cascade:allergyCategoryFrom and cascade:onsetDateFrom). A
# value no member states, such as the highest criticality among them, has no From.
# A member's values link nodes the view builds, each holding values of its own: a time its source wrote short of the
# second (cascade:paddedDateTime), a reference bound (cascade:referenceRangeLow, cascade:referenceRangeHigh), a
# structured dosage (cascade:structuredDosage) and its dose quantity (cascade:dosageDoseQuantity). The link is a row of the member's
# values, with no Part, and each value the node holds is a row with the member's From and Lead and, as Part, the way to
# the node from the member's values, which a reader follows without the node's IRI: the link's local name and, for a
# kind of which one member holds several, a space and what tells them apart (a dosage by its number in its source, as
# pod/My active medications writes it; a padded time by the property it is written for), and for a node under a node
# the same of its link after a slash: `referenceRangeHigh`, `paddedDateTime onsetDate`, `structuredDosage 2` and
# `structuredDosage 2/dosageDoseQuantity`. A value is as the view holds it. A node is two links deep at most; the
# entry's own nodes of these kinds repeat its members' and are not shown. A later kind of node is one more link in the
# path of the first branch's second pattern and, when one member holds several of it, one more branch of the two IFs
# that tell them apart, which read the node's name, the view having made it of its holder's name, a marker and what
# tells the node apart.
PREFIX cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/cascade#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT DISTINCT ?entry ?entryLabel ?view ?field ?value ?valueLabel ?from ?fromLabel ?lead ?part
WHERE {
  { GRAPH ?view { ?entry cascade:entryMember [] ; cascade:leadMember ?leader ; cascade:memberCurrentValues ?values .
                  ?values cascade:valuesOfMember ?from .
                  { ?values ?field ?value FILTER (?field != cascade:valuesOfMember) }
                  UNION
                  { ?values (cascade:paddedDateTime|cascade:referenceRangeLow|cascade:referenceRangeHigh|cascade:structuredDosage|cascade:dosageDoseQuantity)+ ?node .
                    ?holder ?link ?node .
                    OPTIONAL { ?values ?outer ?holder }
                    FILTER (?holder = ?values || BOUND(?outer))
                    BIND (CONCAT(IF(BOUND(?outer),
                                    CONCAT(STRAFTER(STR(?outer), "#"),
                                           IF(?outer = cascade:structuredDosage, CONCAT(" ", STRAFTER(STR(?holder), CONCAT(STR(?values), "-dosage-"))),
                                              IF(?outer = cascade:paddedDateTime, CONCAT(" ", STRAFTER(STR(?holder), CONCAT(STR(?values), "-padded-"))), "")),
                                           "/"),
                                    ""),
                                 STRAFTER(STR(?link), "#"),
                                 IF(?link = cascade:structuredDosage, CONCAT(" ", STRAFTER(STR(?node), CONCAT(STR(?holder), "-dosage-"))),
                                    IF(?link = cascade:paddedDateTime, CONCAT(" ", STRAFTER(STR(?node), CONCAT(STR(?holder), "-padded-"))), ""))) AS ?part)
                    ?node ?field ?value } }
    BIND (?from = ?leader AS ?lead)
    OPTIONAL { ?from rdfs:label ?fromLabel }
    OPTIONAL { ?entry rdfs:label ?entryLabel }
    OPTIONAL { ?value rdfs:label ?valueLabel } }
  UNION
  { GRAPH ?view { ?entry cascade:entryMember [] ; ?field ?value
                  FILTER (!STRSTARTS(STR(?value), CONCAT(STR(?entry), "-")))
                  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?entry cascade:memberCurrentValues ?held . ?held ?field ?value } }
    OPTIONAL { ?entry rdfs:label ?entryLabel }
    OPTIONAL { ?value rdfs:label ?valueLabel } }
}
ORDER BY ?entryLabel ?entry ?field DESC(?lead) STR(?value) ?from ?part
